  - key: tutorial.build.title
    text: 1. Build
  - key: tutorial.build.body
    text: Open Build on the bottom dock and place a Lumber Camp, then a Refinery
      and a Warehouse. Tap a building to use or upgrade it. Its build icon opens
      construction jobs and crew recruitment. Jobs continue while you are away.
  - key: tutorial.storage.title
    text: 3. Store
  - key: tutorial.storage.body
    text: Cargo space is limited. Tap a Warehouse to move stacks between local storage
      and your ship. A working Cargo Depot connects local storage for eligible costs.
      Stock on another world must still be retrieved or transferred.
  - key: tutorial.gather.title
    text: 2. Harvest
  - key: tutorial.gather.body
    text: Tap a Lumber Camp, Mining Rig or another harvester, then HARVEST a resource.
      Collect the result to bring it aboard. The Mining Rig also gathers surface
      scrap.
  - key: tutorial.refine.title
    text: 4. Craft and fuel up
  - key: tutorial.refine.body
    text: Tap a Refinery or crafting station to turn raw resources into fuel and
      parts. Recipes may need research or a higher station level. Fuel powers flights
      and called waves; keep a reserve before departing.
  - key: tutorial.defend.title
    text: 5. Defend and earn XP
  - key: tutorial.defend.body
    text: Tap the Alarm and spend fuel to call a wave. More fuel means a longer fight
      and bigger rewards. Gunners and Lasers defend automatically. Clearing waves
      earns player XP; XP levels unlock higher research and equipment tiers.
  - key: tutorial.research.title
    text: 6. Research technology
  - key: tutorial.research.body
    text: Build a Research Lab from Build > Utility, then open Research > Tech. Each
      technology shows its XP level, local lab level, prerequisites and material
      cost. Upgrade the lab when required. Research unlocks buildings, recipes and
      equipment; Research > Improvements holds global defense and logistics upgrades.
  - key: tutorial.travel.title
    text: 8. Explore
  - key: tutorial.travel.body
    text: Open Map on the bottom dock and spend fuel to visit new planets. Your bases
      stay where you built them. Check deposits and landing hazards before departure;
      upgrade range, scanner and hull protection in Ship > Systems when needed.
  - key: tutorial.map.title
    text: Reading the map
  - key: tutorial.map.body
    text: Tap a world to see its resources, landing hazards and travel cost. Drag
      or pinch to explore. Move within scanner range to reveal deposits. Pin location
      keeps a world in your saved list. Manual flight rewards good piloting; Autopilot
      skips the flight at a higher fuel cost with no refund. Ship > Systems has range,
      scanner and hull upgrades.
  - key: tutorial.upgrade.title
    text: 7. Upgrade
  - key: tutorial.upgrade.body
    text: Ship > Cargo expands carried capacity, Tools improves harvesting, and Systems
      upgrades fuel tanks, engine, range, scanner and hull protection. Tap buildings
      to upgrade their output or services. Harvest and craft the materials for your
      next upgrade.
  - key: tutorial.expand.title
    text: 9. Expand and repeat
  - key: tutorial.expand.body
    text: Establish harvesters, storage and crafting on new worlds for rarer materials.
      Bring those materials back into research and upgrades to reach farther. Tap
      a missing-material cost to find a source. Tap a project's star to track it,
      tap again to stop, and use the star below the top bar to reopen your project.
  - key: about.title
    text: FRONTIER
  - key: about.body
    text: Build bases across the stars. Gather, refine, travel, and defend your worlds
      from alien waves.
