  - key: ranks.unavailable
    text: Online ranks are unavailable until Unity services, a leaderboard and an
      HTTPS privacy policy are configured and approved. Your local record remains
      available above.
  - key: ranks.enable
    text: Anyone can rank. Enabling online ranks connects to Unity using an anonymous
      player ID and posts your Frontier Score. No public name, email or birthday
      is needed. Unity also receives connection data such as your IP address. You
      can turn online services off in Privacy Settings.
  - key: ranks.online.help
    text: Post your current Frontier Score and load the top 20. Your own rank is
      shown even outside the top 20. All players use anonymous pilot labels. These
      are casual, client-reported scores, not cheat-proof competitive rankings.
